The key insight is that valid escape sequences like `_x0061_` will have the 
pattern:
- `\x00_` (underscore in UTF-16-BE)
- `\x00x` (x in UTF-16-BE)
- `\x00` followed by a hex digit (each hex digit is preceded by `\x00` in 
UTF-16-BE)
- `\x00_` (underscore in UTF-16-BE)

But in the case of `_x\u6100\u6200\u6300\u6400_`, the characters after `\x00x` 
are not hex digits preceded by `\x00`, they're actual Unicode characters.

