- Changed to: `rb"\x00_\x00x((?:\x00[a-fA-F0-9]){4})\x00_"`
- This explicitly matches UTF-16-BE byte sequences where each hex digit is 
preceded by `\x00`
- This ensures that valid Unicode escape sequences (e.g., 
`_x\u6100\u6200\u6300\u6400_`) remain preserved without alteration

### 2. Created new `_replace_stderr_clixml` function in 
`/app/lib/ansible/plugins/shell/powershell.py`
- Accepts bytes `stderr` input and returns bytes
- Scans for CLIXML headers matching `b"#< CLIXML\r\n"`
- Detects when a CLIXML sequence starts and ends
- Decodes CLIXML data as UTF-8, with cp437 fallback if UTF-8 decoding fails
- Parses CLIXML content using `_parse_clixml`
- Replaces the original CLIXML block with the decoded text
- Preserves any surrounding data (including trailing bytes on the same line)
- Handles parsing errors or incomplete CLIXML blocks by leaving the original 
data unchanged
- Handles CLIXML blocks split across lines by leaving them unchanged

